# =============================================================================
# TEMPLATE ONLY — copy this file to ".env" and fill in real values.
# Never commit ".env" (it is gitignored). Never put production secrets in GitHub.
# =============================================================================
#
# Prisma requires both values below to be valid Postgres URLs. Each must start with
#   postgresql://   or   postgres://
# (If Prisma says the URL does not start with postgresql://, the variable is empty,
#  malformed, or was pasted incorrectly in Vercel or your local .env.)
#
# === How Prisma uses these (schema: datasource db) ===
# - DATABASE_URL  → env("DATABASE_URL") → Prisma Client (Next.js API, `prisma db seed`)
# - DIRECT_URL    → env("DIRECT_URL") → `prisma migrate deploy` / `migrate dev`
#
# === Local machine (.env on your PC) ===
# Prefer Supabase direct host db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432 for BOTH variables
# when seeding or if the pooler fails locally. URL-encode special characters in the password.
#
# Example (local — same URI twice):
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:ENCODED_PASSWORD@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:ENCODED_PASSWORD@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"
#
# === Vercel (dashboard env vars — Production / Preview) ===
# DATABASE_URL = transaction pooler, port 6543, ?pgbouncer=true
# DIRECT_URL   = direct or session URI on port 5432 (for migrations in CI/build)
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<ref>:PASSWORD@<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connect_timeout=30"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres"
#
# Verify after filling local .env:
#   npx prisma generate
#   npx prisma migrate status
#   npm run db:seed
#
# === App passwords (optional — set on Vercel for production) ===
# These are NOT stored in Supabase; they are checked in Next.js API routes.
# - ADMIN_PASSWORD — /admin-lock and admin-only pages (default in code if unset)
# - ORDER_SUBMIT_PASSWORD — confirm-order modal on store order forms (default: BIGBLUE if unset)
#
# ADMIN_PASSWORD="your-admin-secret"
# ORDER_SUBMIT_PASSWORD="your-order-submit-secret"
